  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 9.4.0 - Add --json flag support (curl 7.82+ compatibility)\nNEW: --json flag support (GitHub Issue #32)\n   - Shorthand for --data with Content-Type: application/json and Accept: application/json\n   - Supports @filename syntax to read JSON from files\n   - Supports --json=data inline syntax\n   - Multiple --json flags concatenate without separator (matching curl behavior)\n   - Works with -X PUT/PATCH/DELETE method overrides\n   - 26 new unit tests covering all scenarios\nCLARIFIED: CurlDotNet never calls curl.exe (GitHub Issue #33)\n   - Pure .NET transpiler - no external process dependencies\n   - Works in any .NET environment including restricted containers\nFrameworks: netstandard2.0, net472, net48, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0\nSponsored by IronSoftware\n\nDocumentation: https://jacob-mellor.github.io/curl-dot-net/\nRepository: https://github.com/jacob-mellor/curl-dot-net\nNuGet: https://www.nuget.org/packages/CurlDotNet/",
